    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.files\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nI've tried every \"oil\" like plugin I can try, and didn't like any of them until yours. I LOVE how you made it so minimal yet flexible\r\n\r\nI do a lot of file renaming and slicing which this is god-tier at doing. There is only one problem, lets say I have these files:\r\n\r\n```\r\n/20231007205727_create_sender_profiles.rb\r\n/20231007211310_create_seed_rounds.rb\r\n/20231007211857_create_seed_round_campaigns.rb\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is a contrived example but I also encounter lots of other situations where i need to copy from PART of a name.\r\n\r\nAnd I want to move the 3rd line to position 1.\r\n\r\nIf I do `vt_` it works great. Then I do my slicing. Now the cursor is right before the `_`, and I hit `h` a whole bunch of times (yes `0` is faster but sometimes muscle memory hard to fight against)\r\n\r\nNow annoyingly I find myself in the root of my harddrive.\r\n\r\nBottom line: This plugin is so perfect for using movement keys to edit files as if theyre a buffer, yet simultaneously blocks usage of keys to do that (movement left right)\r\n\r\nI know I can remap the keys, so that's not an issue. I will probably end up doing that, when I decide what they should be.\r\n\r\nBut it would be cool to have a feature of preventing from going outside my project root that it was originally defined with, or is currently configured in the neovim session.\r\n\r\nIs that an easy feature to add? So mashing `h` bunch of times would never step beyond the root cwd.\r\n",
