            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion and kind words!\r\n\r\nI don't think adding any kind of restriction on movement is a good idea here. Mostly because initial path in `open()` is intentionally has very small effect on overall explorer (it serves as \"root\" to navigate to when lost and to store history of explorer view). Besides, I *have* found myself many times going out of that root directory.\r\n\r\nUse case you describe doesn't seem to be enough to implement this behavior, as there is a [documented suggested solution](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e9a0716013abb8d2d6f8d77331600fb99eb15d51/doc/mini-files.txt#L587-L593) to the problem of pressing `h`/`l` with intention of updating buffer text and not explorer state. I tend to use default mappings and arrows if I want to navigate by character or 'mini.jump'/'mini.jump2d' to jump directly where I need.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
